# ── aienv private configuration - copy to .env (NEVER commit) ─────────────────
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
# Values here are passed into the sandbox with --env-file at creation, exactly
# like <project>/.env - the file that ships a project-scoped token around.

# GitHub fine-grained PAT (one per project preferred, in <project>/.env);
# limit it to the single repository it needs to touch.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# NOTE: no NetBird anything here. The HOST is your only mesh peer and the
# sandboxes reach the AI server through the host-side proxy (see README).
